# Frontend environment variables (Vite)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How production environment files/variables work:
# - Vite exposes ONLY variables prefixed with VITE_ to client-side code (import.meta.env).
#   Never put secrets here; anything VITE_* is bundled into the frontend and public.
# - Local dev: copy to `.env.local` or `.env` in frontend/ as needed (gitignored).
# - Production (Vercel): set these in Vercel Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
#   Vite reads them at BUILD time, so changing them requires a redeploy/rebuild.
# - Backend (Render): must allow this frontend origin via FRONTEND_URL/CORS_ORIGIN and
#   provide PORT/MONGO_URI in Render's environment settings (not committed .env files).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the deployed backend API/Socket.io server on Render (no trailing slash).
# Local dev can leave empty to use Vite proxy/same-origin during development.
VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-service.onrender.com
